			Topic: On EQ2, WoW and the next generation... &nbsp;(Read 992 times)
		</td>
	</tr>
</table>
<table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="bordercolor">
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=174" title="View the profile of Delheru">Delheru</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Hill Giant<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 120<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/blank.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=174"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1199.msg12763#msg12763"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1199.msg12763#msg12763">Re: On EQ2, WoW and the next generation...</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #15 on:</b> November 19, 2004, 01:47:10 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1199.msg12557#msg12557">Quote from: Zerxes on November 12, 2004, 01:38:26 pm</a></div><div class="quote">Don&#039;t hold your breath on Vanguard.</div>I&#039;m not holding my breath, but they have the balls to do a lot of things right, even though they are difficult. Can&#039;t help loving them for that.<br /> <br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote"> A return to long corpse recoveries, long travel times</div>WoW has both in many ways. Especially when the spirit res fucked up all your gear, CR could be really exciting indeed. Not sure why Vanguard would be so extremely different in this. Have you ever flown the, mmm, Night Elf area -&gt; Feralas flight with a griffon? It&#039;s over 12 minutes just flying. I don&#039;t mind it, but from the way you write about it, I would imagine you would.<br /><br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">non-instanced dungeons that result in groups camping various rooms of the dungeon, etc. is not going to bring back the magic people are longing for.</div>Non-instanced halle-fucking-lujah. I _HATE_ instancing. Hate hate hate hate hate. If I want an instanced game I&#039;ll play Baldur&#039;s Gate with my friends or something, I&#039;ll get lower ping too. MMORPG is not supposed to be gamespy+baldur&#039;s gate or whatever. The world needs to be real, and having Eranikus (baddest mob of the time in beta) die like every 2 minutes on a single server (I shit you not) sorta ripped out the magic.<br /><br />Not to mention social cockblock in the form of other players totally owns 100% artificial cockblocks.<br /><br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote"> I&#039;ve said it a few times now and I&#039;ll say it again:  I&#039;m convinced many MMORPG -gamers are simply trying to recapture the magic that existed in their first MMORPG.  All of us have lost our MMORPG virginity, and that is something we will never get back.</div>It just needs something radical. That means working collision code, working AI or a truly dynamic world. Any one of those three done in a well executed game and you&#039;d certainly recapture the magic.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg12905"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=179" title="View the profile of Kelce">Kelce</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Hill Giant<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 112<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/megatron.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								Asshole.<br />
								<br />
								
								<a href="http://members.msn.com/kelce@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/msntalk.gif" alt="kelce@hotmail.com" border="0" /></a>
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=179"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://www.shadowsanddust.org" title="Linkz" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/www_sm.gif" alt="WWW" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:haplessrogue@gmail.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1199.msg12905#msg12905"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1199.msg12905#msg12905">Re: On EQ2, WoW and the next generation...</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #16 on:</b> December 01, 2004, 09:23:54 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">Have you ever flown the, mmm, Night Elf area -&gt; Feralas flight with a griffon? It&#039;s over 12 minutes just flying. I don&#039;t mind it, but from the way you write about it, I would imagine you would.</div> Haven&#039;t, however the Zoram Strand to... anywhere is the longest flight I&#039;ve had to perform yet, still awaiting some of the Horde&#039;s TransAzerothan flights to Booty Bay and such. Those seem long, however they&#039;ll also provide a chance to get up and stretch, etc. In short; I like the forced waits of these flights.<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">The world needs to be real, and having Eranikus (baddest mob of the time in beta) die like every 2 minutes on a single server (I shit you not) sorta ripped out the magic.</div>The instances I have enjoyed so far (Wailing, Ragefire, Shadowfang and Kraul) have been enjoyable. WC is so far, the most pleased with a dungeon&#039;s design yet. However I do miss dungeons like Sebilis and Guk where fighting for spawns would occur. Not so much a social cockblock as it would allow more interaction, even with the assholes of the server.<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">It just needs something radical. That means working collision code, working AI or a truly dynamic world. Any one of those three done in a well executed game and you&#039;d certainly recapture the magic.</div> As a warrior, it&#039;s the abilities. I can choose not to spam taunt but use abilities to keep agro (sunder works, so does Retaliation to start a fight).
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg12943"></a>
